<title>SINGAPORE: Pacific carriers 1996 net falls 30 pct.</title>
<headline>Pacific carriers 1996 net falls 30 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			     19.79 vs   28.47</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)			4.00 vs    4.00</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		     6.60 vs    9.49</p>
<p>    Turnover				122.06 vs  137.35</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	 2.10 vs    1.29</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		    0.01 vs    0.97</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortisation	  12.85 vs   16.92</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			 12.97 vs   11.84</p>
<p>    Profits from associates	    11.14 vs   20.02</p>
<p>    Tax					 4.32 vs    3.63</p>
<p>    Minorities				nil  vs    0.24 (gain)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries	     (loss)  0.08 vs    0.30 (gain)</p>
<p>    Dividend pay date:    June 27, 1997</p>
<p>Last day books open:  June 16, 1997</p>
<p>Note - Pacific Carriers Ltd is a shipping group.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
